<p style="font-size:15px">
<h4>Results</h4>

<h5><b>Prophylactic Vaccination</b></h5>
<p>The results table provides detailed information on the forecasted vaccination requirements for different countries, years, and species. Here's a breakdown of each column:</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Country</strong>: This column lists the country for which the forecast is made.</li>
  <li><strong>Year</strong>: This column indicates the specific year for which the forecasted data applies.</li>
  <li><strong>Species</strong>: This column specifies the type of livestock (e.g., cattle, sheep) for which the forecast is generated.</li>
  <li><strong>Forecasted Value</strong>: This column shows the predicted population of the specified species in the given country and year, based on historical data and the AutoEnsemble model.</li>
  <li><strong>Youngstock Coverage</strong>: This column displays the number of vaccine doses required for young livestock (e.g., calves, lambs).</li>
  <li><strong>Adult Coverage</strong>: This column indicates the number of vaccine doses required for adult livestock.</li>
  <li><strong>Vaccine Requirement</strong>: This column provides the total estimated number of vaccine doses needed to achieve the forecasted coverage for both youngstock and adult livestock.</li>
</ul>

<p>By understanding these columns, you can effectively interpret the forecasted vaccination needs and make informed decisions for your livestock management and disease control strategies.</p>
<br><br>

